  "description": "LUYFOB crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H143 N6 O17 S10 Sm4 3+,3(N1 O3 1-),2(C3 H7 N1 O1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm1B (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm2B (Sm) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.634-5.206 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.70-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C102H143N6O17S10Sm4·3(NO3)·2(dmf)·3(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
